          ],
          "content": "Ganita Prakash | Grade 7"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.206,
            0.087,
            0.466,
            0.108
          ],
          "content": "(a) Largest multiple of 5"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.207,
            0.112,
            0.481,
            0.132
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "(b) Smallest even number"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.136,
            0.848,
            0.193
          ],
          "content": "2. The number 10,30,285 in words is Ten lakhs thirty thousand two hundred eighty five, which has 42 letters. Give a 7-digit number name which has the maximum number of letters."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.197,
            0.848,
            0.236
          ],
          "content": "3. Write a 9-digit number where exchanging any two digits results in a bigger number. How many such numbers exist?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.239,
            0.848,
            0.278
          ],
          "content": "4. Strike out 10 digits from the number 12345123451234512345 so that the remaining number is as large as possible."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.282,
            0.849,
            0.357
          ],
          "content": "5. The words ‘zero’ and ‘one’ share letters ‘e’ and ‘o’. The words ‘one’ and ‘two’ share a letter ‘o’, and the words ‘two’ and ‘three’ also share a letter ‘t’. How far do you have to count to find two consecutive numbers which do not share an English letter in common?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.361,
            0.814,
            0.418
          ],
          "content": "6. Suppose you write down all the numbers 1, 2, 3, 4, …, 9, 10, 11, ... The tenth digit you write is ‘1’ and the eleventh digit is ‘0’, as part of the number 10."
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.829,
            0.347,
            0.93,
            0.403
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_19_image_8.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.206,
            0.422,
            0.848,
            0.46
          ],
          "content": "(a) What would the 1000th digit be? At which number would it occur?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.206,
            0.463,
            0.74,
            0.485
          ],
          "content": "(b) What number would contain the millionth digit?"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.206,
            0.488,
            0.812,
            0.526
          ],
          "content": "(c) When would you have written the digit ‘5’ for the 5000th time?"
        },
        {
          "type": "image",
          "bbox": [
            0.827,
            0.47,
            0.93,
            0.527
          ],
          "content": "",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_19_image_12.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.151,
            0.531,
            0.849,
            0.588
          ],
          "content": "7. A calculator has only ‘+10,000’ and ‘+100’ buttons. Write an expression describing the number of button clicks to be made for the following numbers:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.207,
            0.592,
            0.325,
            0.613
          ],
          "content": "(a) 20,800"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.206,
            0.615,
            0.326,
            0.636
          ],
          "content": "(b) 92,100"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.207,
            0.639,
            0.343,
            0.661
          ],
          "content": "(c) 1,20,500"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.207,
            0.663,
            0.353,
            0.685
          ],
          "content": "(d) 65,30,000"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.207,
            0.688,
            0.353,
            0.709
          ],
          "content": "(e) 70,25,700"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.15,
            0.712,
            0.517,
            0.732
          ],
          "content": "8. How many lakhs make a billion?"
